# Testing Rules

- Use pytest for all tests.
- Target code coverage > 90%.
- Test behavior, not implementation details.
- Cover:
  - Happy paths
  - Edge cases
  - Validation failures
  - Error handling paths
- Use fixtures to reduce duplication.
- Mock external APIs, databases, file systems, and third-party services.
- Tests must be deterministic and independent.
- Follow Arrange-Act-Assert structure.
- Prefer parametrized tests for multiple scenarios.
- Keep tests simple, readable, and maintainable.
- Every bug fix should include a regression test.
- Avoid unnecessary mocking of internal application code.
- Verify retry, timeout, and rate-limiting behavior when applicable.
